**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** An import profile is a named mapping of a lab file's layout and columns, stored in the kit file (001 §K 'save the mapping as a named import profile in `.kit-json`'; 001 §E 'The kit file holds … the import profiles'; step 122: 'S9.2 the import profiles'; 001 §K 'Raw data is immutable': an experiment names its profile, step 291, so a saved profile is never replaced). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.2. In `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, after `DataColumnNumber` (step 298) and before `NamingTemplate`, in this order: (1) `ScanColumn = { column : DataColumnNumber; valueUnit : ScanColumnUnit; reading : ScanReading }`, a column of a scan variable's values; a profile's scan columns, in column order, give the experiment's scan quantities in order (step 304). (2) `ReadingColumns` = `SignalColumns of signal : DataColumnNumber * sigmaOpt : DataColumnNumber option` (a detector signal and its σ) | `MuellerElementColumns of elements : DataColumnNumber list * throughputOpt : DataColumnNumber option` (the sixteen elements m00…m33 in row order, and the absolute throughput when the elements are normalized): what each row measured. (3) `ColumnRoles = { scan : ScanColumn list; reading : ReadingColumns; timestampOpt : DataColumnNumber option; captureIndexOpt : DataColumnNumber option; observableOpt : DataColumnNumber option; keyOpt : DataColumnNumber option }`, every role a column holds (001 §K): the scan variables, the reading, the capture's timestamp and index, the observable (T or R) and the experiment key that splits one file into experiments (S9.3). (4) `ImportProfileError`, an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string`: `BlankProfileNameErr` (a profile name holding only white space), `BuiltInProfileNameErr` (a built-in profile's name), `DuplicateProfileNameErr` (a name the kit's profiles hold), `SignalColumnCountErr` (a signal mapping with no signal column or more than one), `MixedReadingColumnsErr` (a mapping with a signal and Mueller elements), `RepeatedRoleErr` (a one-column role given to two columns) and `MuellerElementCountErr` (a Mueller mapping that does not give each of m00…m33 exactly one column). `member this.describe : string` renders each in step 39's form: `the import profile name is blank: <reason>`, `the name belongs to a built-in import profile: <reason>`, `the kit already holds an import profile of that name: <reason>`, `a signal mapping needs exactly one signal column: <reason>`, `a mapping reads a signal or Mueller elements, not both: <reason>`, `a role is given to two columns: <reason>` and `a Mueller mapping needs each of m00…m33 once: <reason>`. (5) `ImportProfile = { name : ImportProfileName; delimiter : DataDelimiter; header : HeaderRowChoice; bom : ByteOrderMark; roles : ColumnRoles }`, one named mapping of a lab file; the four built-in profiles are code and never stored (step 300). (6) `type ImportProfileName with member this.availableAmong (profiles : ImportProfile list) : Result<ImportProfileName, ImportProfileError>`, the one naming rule of a new profile: a name of `builtIns` answers `BuiltInProfileNameErr` and a name ordinal-equal to a held profile's `DuplicateProfileNameErr`, each naming it; any other answers itself. (7) `KitFile` (step 122) gains `importProfiles : ImportProfile list` after `namingTemplate` (step 267), and `KitFile.create` sets it to `[]`, so `KitFolder.namedKitFile` (step 145) and `scratchKit` (step 150) take it unchanged; `member this.withImportProfile (profile : ImportProfile) : Result<KitFile, ImportProfileError>` on `KitFile` is `profile.name.availableAmong this.importProfiles`, whose `Ok` appends the profile. (8) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/kit.schema.json` (steps 124, 267): under `if` `schemaVersion` is 1, `importProfiles` joins the required keys as an array of objects, each with exactly the required keys `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character), `delimiter` (an integer 1 to 3), `header` (1 to 2), `bom` (1 to 2) and `roles`, an object with exactly the keys `scan` (an array of objects of exactly `column`, an integer of at least 1, `valueUnit`, 1 to 6, and `reading`, 1 to 2), `reading` (an object) and the four `…Opt` keys (each an integer of at least 1 or `null`); `additionalProperties: false` holds at each level. The schema version stays 1, because kit files of the old shape exist only under test output (.spec-md §7). No up-converter, default-on-read, replace or delete verb is added. Tests. `KitTests` gains `a profile name is refused when a built-in or a kit profile holds it, and a kit file appends a new profile`: over a test-local signal profile `Lab scan` (comma, a header row, no byte-order mark; scan column 1 in degrees as a physical value; `SignalColumns (2, Some 3)`; key column 4; no timestamp, capture index or observable column), step 122's `KitFile.create` fixture holds no profile; its `withImportProfile` of `Lab scan` holds exactly it; that kit file's `withImportProfile` of `Lab scan` again answers `DuplicateProfileNameErr` naming `Lab scan`, and of a profile named `Phone ROI CSV` `BuiltInProfileNameErr`; and `(ImportProfileName "lab scan").availableAmong [ <Lab scan> ]` answers itself, the comparison being ordinal. `every import profile error renders its condition and its payload`: each case over a distinct test-local reason renders a distinct text that contains the reason. `KitFileJsonTests` (steps 124, 267), whose kit file now also holds `importProfiles` of `Lab scan` and a test-local Mueller profile `Polarimeter` (tab, no header row, no byte-order mark; scan columns 1 in degrees and 2 in radians, both physical values; `MuellerElementColumns` of columns 3 to 18 with throughput 19; observable 20; key 21): `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` lists the top-level keys `author`, `created`, `id`, `importProfiles`, `modified`, `name`, `namingTemplate`, `notes`, `schemaVersion` and `sendExclude` in that order and writes `Polarimeter`'s `delimiter` as `3`; `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds` also refuses the text without `importProfiles`, with a profile whose `delimiter` is `0`, and with a profile that has no `roles`, each with `SchemaValidationErr`. Every other kit-file fact passes unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the kit file holds import profiles, `ImportProfile` and `ColumnRoles` MUST exist in `Kit.fs`, `KitFile` MUST carry `importProfiles` (empty for a new kit), `KitFile.withImportProfile` MUST append a profile and refuse a built-in's or a held profile's name, and `kit.schema.json` MUST require the profiles; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a profile name is refused when a built-in or a kit profile holds it, and a kit file appends a new profile` and `every import profile error renders its condition and its payload`, the count rising by 2, and the changed `a kit file round-trips through its canonical text` and `a schema-invalid or malformed kit file is refused before it binds`; and build, elevation and the sixteen s30 invariants MUST pass.
